"[2608.30620] On the Nielsen realisation problem for cyclic groups of prime order (https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.30620)\nciteturn6view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.30620\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 160\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Geometric Topology\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 31 Aug 2026]\nL9: # Title:On the Nielsen realisation problem for cyclic groups of prime order\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Christian Kremer L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled On the Nielsen realisation problem for cyclic groups of prime order, by Christian Kremer\nL14: \nL15: cite6†View PDF cite7†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:We solve the Nielsen realisation problem for high-dimensional aspherical manifolds in a new class of special cases. Mainly, we focus on actions of cyclic groups of prime order. A novelty is that it gives topological solutions to the problem with certain high-dimensional fixed point sets, whereas previous solutions of this type were restricted to discrete fixed point sets.\nL17: This is enabled by recent joint work with Kirstein on isovariant Poincaré duality spaces, and Farrell-Lück-Steimle's obstruction theory to finding approximate fibrations within a homotopy class.\nL18: Comments:  | 35 pages, comments welcome\nL19: Subjects:  | Geometric Topology (math.GT)\nL20: Report number:  | MPIM-Bonn-2026\nL21: Cite as:  | cite8†arXiv:2608.30620 [math.GT]\nL22:    | (or cite9†arXiv:2608.30620v1 [math.GT] for this version)\nL23:    | cite10†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2608.30620†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite (pending registration)\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Christian Kremer [cite11†view email 